course: dictionary
lesson: 4529
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Heal is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «A cast stops a broken bone moving while it heals.» The clues are broken bone and cast, so heal means to get healthy again after an injury.
explain: Heal can also mean to make bad feelings or a quarrel better. Nothing is broken in that case, so the clues point to feelings, not the body. Ask yourself: what is being healed? A body, a bone, or a feeling?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «A cast stops a broken bone moving while it becomes healthy again» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If it sounds silly, try the other meaning.
fact: Heal is a verb. Its forms are heals, healed, and healing.
fact: «Heal» means to become healthy again after an injury, like a cut or a broken bone.
fact: «Heal» can also mean to make someone well again.
fact: «Heal» can mean to make bad feelings or a quarrel better.
fact: Keeping a wound clean helps it heal, but picking a scab slows healing down.
exercise: «A cast stops a broken bone moving while it heals.» What does heals mean here? | Gets louder and stronger | Breaks into pieces | *Becomes healthy again after an injury
exercise: Priya says, «Keeping a wound clean helps it heal; picking a scab slows it down.» What does picking a scab do? | It helps the wound heal faster | It turns the scab into new skin at once | *It slows the healing down
exercise: Tom and Sam had a big quarrel. Which sentence uses heal to mean make the bad feeling better? | The plaster helped the cut heal | The doctor will heal the broken arm | *Saying sorry may help to heal the quarrel
test: «Swimmer's ear is an infection of the ear canal; once it has healed, swimming can start again.» What does healed mean here? | Hidden away | *Become healthy again after the infection | Made wet | Left behind
test: Fill the gap: Her leg is ___ slowly after the fall. | *Healing | Heal | Heals | Healed
exam: Which meaning of heal is used in «Some stable ankle breaks heal well in a removable boot instead of a cast»? | Make a quarrel stop | Make bad feelings worse | Shine brightly | *Become healthy again after an injury
